<title>GERMANY: IFO sees moderate growth for German food sector.</title>
<headline>IFO sees moderate growth for German food sector.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's food industry is expected to see a two-percent increase in production and turnover in 1996, a report by IFO, the German economic research institute, said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Increased foreign demand led the growth in the sector, while food producers saw demand stagnate during the year, the IFO report said.</p>
<p>High levels of over-capacity and competition meant that the consumer benefited from low prices, the report said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
